wifi: mt76: mt7925: add TP-Link Archer TBE550E antenna LED support

The TP-Link Archer TBE550E (MT7927, PCI 14c3:7927, subsystem 105b:e104)
has a magnetic antenna base with a light ring. TP-Link's Windows driver
(mtkwecx.sys) drives it only for this card: its INF sets OemLedMode=2,
which selects unified MCU command 0x2a on two GPIO pins hardcoded in the
MT7927 chip profile, pin1=53 and pin2=54. Tag 0 enables a pin, tag 1 sets
its value (1 or 3); four mode combinations are used.

Observed on hardware with TP-Link's firmware (WM build 20250606201037):
mode 0 = off, 1 = breathing, 2 and 3 = steady. With a 2026 firmware build
modes 2/3 did not give a steady light. Colour and the on/off touch switch
are handled by the base itself.

- Add MCU_UNI_CMD_TPLINK_GPIO (0x2a).
- Detect subsystem 105b:e104; module parameters can disable it or
  override the pins.
- Enable both pins on hardware init and restore them on resume.
- Auto mode: steady while associated, breathing otherwise, as TP-Link
  documents for Windows. Redundant updates during association are
  skipped.
- Manual modes are never overridden by link changes or interface stop.
- sysfs: tplink_led_mode (0-3, auto) and tplink_led_pins.
- tplink_led_debug: request a firmware ACK and log it (runtime only).
- Wake the chip before sysfs-triggered MCU commands.

Developed with AI assistance (Claude). Tested by the submitter on a
TBE550E with this package tree (v2.17-2, mt76 from Linux 7.3) built for
kernel 7.0 on Ubuntu 24.04: associates first try, auto mode is steady
while connected, and modes 0/1/2 give off/breathing/steady.

